  "system": {
    "description": {
      "gm": "",
      "value": "<p><span style=\"mso-bidi-font-size:12.0pt;mso-bidi-font-family:Calibri;mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-latin\">Necromantic powers of Synark have seeped in the lands of Zaho, and it awakens in you in the form of transforming you into an undead cazic-fer. In the process, however, your flesh begins to decay, or your form is partially or completely reduced to an animated skeleton. You gain basic undead benefits. Your undead hunger pushes you to collect bones or flesh that you can use to help yourself mend.</span></p><p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span style=\"mso-bidi-font-size:12.0pt;mso-bidi-font-family:Calibri;mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-latin\"><span style=\"text-decoration:underline\">Special:</span></span><span style=\"mso-bidi-font-size:12.0pt;mso-bidi-font-family:Calibri;mso-bidi-theme-font:minor-latin\"> If you are using the Golarion Ancestries rule, you can select any Skeleton ancestry feats (at your GM’s discretion).</span></p>"
